## Key Concepts

- CKNE-to-quotas mapping (connections, buffers, priorities)
- Real-time reallocation cadence (minute granularity)
- Per-tenant isolation in a shared socket pool
- Observability and SLA guarantees

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo CKNE balancer skeleton
class CKNEBalancer {
  constructor(baseline) {
    this.quotas = new Map();
    this.baseline = baseline;
  }
  quotaFor(tenant) {
    return this.quotas.get(tenant) ?? this.baseline;
  }
  adjust(mBurst, ckne) {
    // simple proportional adjustment
    // higher CKNE -> more quota, lower CKNE -> less
  }
}
